{
<tab><cl=F0F010>GETTING A MISSION<cl=A2A2A2><br><br>
<tab>In the window of receiving the mission key, you can select the type of mission, its location and the number of participants. The following types of missions are distinguished:<br>
<tab><cl=FFFFFF>A mission for the title<cl=B0B0B0>. Upon successful completion, you will receive title stamps.<br>
<tab><cl=FFFFFF>The mission for the degree<cl=B0B0B0>. Upon successful completion, you will receive degree stamps.<br>
<tab><cl=FFFFFF>A mission for money<cl=B0B0B0>. Upon successful completion, you will receive a cash reward.<br>
<tab><cl=FFFFFF>A mission for karma<cl=B0B0B0>. Upon successful completion, your karma will improve.<br><br>
<tab>The location of the mission can be either "nearby" or on one of the continents. When you take a mission located "nearby", you are guaranteed to find it near the place where you received the mission key. However, in this case, your reward will be 3-4 times less.<br>
<tab>The number of mission participants can vary from 1 to 4. The complexity of the mission increases proportionally. At the time of completion of the mission, everyone who is currently in the area of the achieved goal (for example, in a dungeon) receives a reward. The taken mission should be received by all participants. To do this, one participant takes the mission key, and then <cl=FFFFFF>applies<cl=B0B0B0> it to the rest. The key is duplicated an unlimited number of times. You can take five missions for two. The reward will be divided into the corresponding number of participants.<br>
<tab>Keep in mind that the mission key burns out in about a day by Sphere time (2 hours by Earth time).<br>
<tab>You won't be able to take the mission key if you already have one. You will also not be able to get rid of the received mission key until it expires.<br>
<tab>The mission description can be read by <cl=FFFFFF>looking<cl=B0B0B0> at the mission key.<br>
}